hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"487","Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Malik, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, shall I seek permission to enter upon my mother? He said: Yes. The man said: I live with her in the house. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Would you like to see her naked? He said: No. He said: Then seek permission to enter upon her."
"488","Nusayr ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Amr informed us, that Safwan ibn Sulaym informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umm Ayman, who is the mother of Usamah: How are you this morning, or how are you this evening? She said: Well, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Amen; may Allah keep you well."
"489","Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of a group gives greeting, it suffices for them. Abu Dawud said: And it has been narrated with a connected chain, but it is weak."
"490","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Mushir, from al-Ajlah, from al-Sha'bi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Ja'far ibn Abi Talib, embraced him, and kissed him between his eyes. Abu Dawud said: This has been narrated with a connected chain but it is not sound."
